  "body": "Found in the #626 lathe investigation.\n\n**Today:** with the shipped `assets/machines/lathe.mch`, X travel is `0..320`. Threading CL half-turns reach the antipode at negative X (e.g. \"move 2 reaches -6.050 in X\"), so the machine-limit gate refuses every thread on the built-in Lathe. The investigation had to use the TestBench machine from `lathe_post_g76.rs`.\n\n**Expected:** either the limit check judges a lathe thread's posted diameter rather than the CL antipode, or lathe.mch states the band the CL needs. Decide which is correct; the antipode is a CL artifact the post never writes.\n\n**Done means:** a thread on the built-in Lathe machine posts, and a real over-travel on that machine is still refused by name.",
